"""tinycap: the broader capability suite on the SERVED steerable path, on
Modal H200s — one container per configuration, under the Modal app the wave
NAMES (``TINYCAP_APP_NAME=<name>`` in the environment + ``--app-name <name>``;
there is no default app, E40 M7).

ONE INVOCATION IS ONE MODEL. ``--model <slug>`` selects a row of
``contracts.MODELS`` (default ``gemma4e4b``); ``--cells`` takes any cell the
serving grammar accepts (``none``, ``prompted__<si>``, ``<si>__<arm>``);
``--modes`` takes ``off`` / ``on`` / ``per-task``; ``--app-name`` names the
wave in the dashboard. The four original gemma configurations are still exactly
what the default arguments plan.

The two Gemma-4-E4B test cells (prompted safety SI; safety psr_kl object) x
thinking {off, on} = four configurations, ONE H200 container each. Every
steered number goes through the
served declared-response-prefill path (E6): the in-tree standup
``scripts/capctrl_serving_up.py`` (lens vLLM + RoutingProxy), then the
usage-ledger proxy (``sisteer.capeval.serving.usage_ledger``) on loopback
IN FRONT of the RoutingProxy, then ``scripts/served_capability_run.py``
with the argv ``contracts.driver_argv`` builds (``--thinking``, ``--samples``,
``--inspect-limit``, ``--ledger-url``; every name from
``sisteer.capeval.tinycap.contracts``, never retyped).

Per configuration (as amended by the 2026-09-03 staging and
the battery changes of 2026-09-04 and 2026-09-06 and the one of
2026-09-07 —
``CONTROLS_PROMPTED`` / ``CONTROLS_FITTED`` are the ``--pass1`` defaults: the
STANDARD battery of ``contracts.battery_controls`` with the staging exclusions
applied, so an operator types no control list; ``--in-depth`` adds
``contracts.IN_DEPTH_EXTRAS`` — MATH-500 avg@4 and the FULL 1,319-item GSM8K,
both set aside for now; ``--controls`` still overrides
everything):
  prompted x off : (no standup extras)              the standard GSM8K (the paired-200
                                                     subset, U4(a)), HE+, OR-Bench
  prompted x on  : --reasoning-parser gemma4          same (+ :open code variants)
  psrkl x off    : (no standup extras)              the SAME battery (O7)
  psrkl x on     : --reasoning-parser gemma4          same
U1's fitted-cell hold (tiny ONLY until the server-side hooked-decode fix) ended
with E23 / PW15: the vectorized lens landed and the fitted generation runs went
out at 1983322, so the fitted default is its full standard battery.
The 2026-09-07 change dropped the two GENERATIVE letter-choice legs — ``inspect_cmp:mmlu`` and
``hellaswag_inspect`` — because the prefill-only letter reads were then the
knowledge / sentence-completion instrument and a generative twin of the same
eval must not run (that loglikelihood family was itself removed later, with the
third-party harness it ran on); a change of 2026-09-11 then retired both from the
grammar altogether (with the full 3,981-item ``bfcl``; ``bfcl_200`` stays).
``inspect_cmp:xstest`` is out of every default list with status
``unavailable_gated`` (``EXCLUDED_DEFAULT_CONTROLS``): ``walledai/XSTest``
403s for every token this workspace holds (stage 2026-09-03); the dry run
prints the exclusion, and an operator with access names it in ``--controls``.
Since U14 that exclusion narrows no default — the battery names the OR-Bench
atom, not the ``inspect_cmp`` family — but it still governs an explicit
``--controls inspect_cmp``.
``--tool-calls`` is composed ONLY when BFCL is among the controls (E3: tool
calling is a server launch option) — and U9 item 6 took BFCL out of the
battery, so NO default configuration composes it any more, prompted or fitted;
``--controls bfcl_200`` (the pinned 200) still does, on either kind of cell.
``--reasoning-parser gemma4`` under thinking-ON (the standup's own
passthrough).

GEOMETRY. Pass 1 runs every configuration at the certified
Petri footprint — ``geometry.pass1_geometry(<sub-entry>)``, which reads the
composer's ``PETRI_MAX_MODEL_LEN x DEFAULT_MAX_NUM_SEQS``; no literal window
lives in this file (tests/test_served_geometry greps for one) — and the
ledger records every attempted call. ``scripts/tinycap_geometry_measure.py``
pools the ledgers into the proposed ``capability:{tiny, tiny_prompted,
gen_long, gen_long_thinking, agent, agent_thinking}`` entries for Evals'
acceptance (plus MATH-500's own per-prompt-class entries ``capability:gen_long_math``
/ ``capability:gen_long_math_longsi``, measured from its prompt budget); pass 2 (``--pass2``) resolves the MEASURED entry through
``resolve_geometry`` and therefore cannot run before it has landed.
ONE exception to the pass-1 footprint: a configuration whose controls
are MATH-500 alone (``--pass1 --controls math500``, a MATH smoke) resolves
MATH-500's entry for the cell's PROMPT CLASS — ``capability:gen_long_math`` for
the bare / safety-SI cells, ``capability:gen_long_math_longsi`` for the
constitution / irrelevant SIs (the pre-allocation fit check holds the
window to THAT class's measured prompt max + the cap) — at its OWN measured
window in pass 1 as in pass 2 — the footprint cannot hold MATH's prompt max + its cap, and the entry is
sized from the prompt budget, not from a ledger a footprint pass would
extend; a configuration that pools MATH-500 beside other sub-entries
(``--in-depth``, ``--controls gsm8k,math500``) is REFUSED by name before any
allocation (``Pass1FootprintCannotHold``: one standup at MATH's window would
size every other key's traffic to a window measured for something else) —
run MATH-500 alone and the rest of the battery without it.
Concurrency = the resolved S, by construction (``--concurrency``).

THE PER-MODEL BUDGET (E7 -> E15; ``geometry.BUDGET_BY_MODEL``, 2026-09-04).
Evals MEASURED gemma4e4b's batched-token budget on one H200 at
gpu-memory-utilization 0.90 (the standup's ``--gpu-mem-util`` below is the
same 0.90) and it is 1.50x the Llama-certified ``BATCHED_TOKEN_BUDGET``, so
the certified footprint's S under-fills the card by a third. The number now
lives in the geometry module (``BUDGET_BY_MODEL``, its basis with it); this
launcher sizes S from it by the contracts' model slug — both passes resolve
with ``model_key`` (``pass1_geometry(..., model_key=)`` /
``resolve_geometry(..., model_key=)``: S = the model's budget at the window
through ``ModelBudget.seqs_at``, ``seqs_source = "model_budget"``, never a
typed S) — passes the standup the explicit dims (a provisional entry cannot
be re-derived from ``--eval``) PLUS ``--model-key`` so the standup's own
budget guard and its ``endpoint.json`` are held to the same model, drives
the client at that S, and writes the budget record + the standup's
``endpoint.json`` into ``<out_dir>/served_geometry.json`` so the measurement
proposal can see the S that was actually served. No ``--allow-over-budget``:
the product IS the model's budget and the identity holds by construction. A
model whose budget is not MEASURED refuses (``UnmeasuredBudget``) — never
the Llama-certified default's S; a key outside ``geometry.MODEL_KEYS``
refuses in the geometry module (``UnknownModelKey``).

IMAGE. Today's capctrl serving image (cu129 vllm 0.25.1 / torch 2.11.0 /
vllm-lens 1.2.1 / transformers 5.14.1) plus a SECOND venv ``/opt/client``
(python 3.12) installed from the fully pinned + hashed lock
``configs/capeval/tinycap-client-requirements.txt`` with ``uv pip install
--no-deps --require-hashes`` — the build FAILS on non-resolution; no version
fallback, no unpinned install (P21). The VCS requirements
(``contracts.CLIENT_VCS_PINS``, each at a full commit) are the only lines uv
cannot hash and are installed separately at exactly those commits. The vLLM venv's own helper
packages are pinned too (R8, ``SERVING_IMAGE_PINS``): every one that the
client lock also carries takes the lock's version (one version of each
across the two venvs) except ``numpy``, whose lock version vllm cannot
install (``SERVING_IMAGE_PINS_OFF_LOCK`` says why); the rest an exact
release at least a week old. ``image_install_specs()`` lists every
requirement the image installs and the launcher test refuses a floating
one. Inspect's openai-v3 /
pydantic>=2.13 / fsspec ceilings never touch the vLLM venv. The driver and
the ledger run in the client venv; the standup runs in the vLLM venv;
sisteer rides on PYTHONPATH in both (the STAGED tree, never the local one).

RESUME (R2, launcher half; E12 item 1). Every store is idempotent; the
driver's task runners write a per-task completion marker ``<cell_dir>/done/
<task with / -> __>.json`` ONLY on a complete, unlimited run
(``tinycap.completion``; a limited run leaves ``partial/<task>.json``
instead). Before ANY marker is read, the configuration's FULL expected
identity is derived from its RESOLVED inputs (``expected_identity``: the
served geometry — window AND S — through ``served_geometry``, the driver's
``--concurrency`` (= S), the parser and tool-call mode the standup argv
composes, the pass number, the avg@k width, the active limits, the staged
tree's client-lock sha). A re-run drops a control only when ONE cell
directory under ``<out_dir>/cells/`` — never a union of bare file names
across directories — is a trusted store for exactly that identity
(``untrusted_store_reason``: the manifest names this cell; its key carries
the manifest's intervention / harness hash prefixes; the recorded
``harness_config_hash`` IS the hash of the recorded ``resolved_config`` and
the ``tinycap`` block mirrors the hashed one; the identity carries EXACTLY
``TINYCAP_IDENTITY_FIELDS`` — a legacy manifest lacking a field is refused,
never read around; ``served`` carries EXACTLY ``SERVED_IDENTITY_FIELDS`` and
equals the expected values per field; the hashed ``tinycap.pass`` AND the
top-level ``geometry.pass`` are this pass (PW8: the pass is identity, so a
pass-2 run never keys onto a pass-1 store);
``thinking.mode``, ``samples``, an EMPTY ``limits``, the frameworks block
(the lock sha, pinned versions), the ``producer`` block, and the manifest's
own geometry / concurrency / thinking / route blocks agreeing with the
hashed identity), the store REQUESTED the control's atoms (``tinycap.tasks``)
AND every task the control produces has a validated done marker there
(exactly ``DONE_MARKER_FIELDS``, the right task, a positive ``n_items`` equal
to the frozen full count where the contracts state one, no partial marker
beside it, and its ``summary/<task>.json`` agreeing on ``n`` — the merge
needs that file). ``resume_report`` names why every other store was not
trusted; it rides in the REC. The standup is skipped entirely when nothing
remains. Ledger rows are append-only. The standup's tool-call mode is
composed from the REQUESTED controls (never the remaining ones) so every
resume of one configuration serves one identity.

TREE_SHA (E12 item 3). ``--upload-tree`` archives the tree with a
``TREE_SHA`` file (``contracts.TREE_SHA_FILENAME``, the full 40-hex commit)
at its root; the stage verifies it, preflight checks it, a configuration
refuses (``NO_TREE_SHA``) without it, and the driver records it as
``manifest.producer.tree_sha`` — the tree that PRODUCED every row.

MERGE (N1 / R3; E12 item 3). ``controls_summary.json`` has one writer,
``tinycap.completion.merge_controls_summary``, which needs
``sisteer.eval.cell_controls`` (torch). The driver runs it after a complete
run (Inspect); the EvalPlus tasks finish LATER, in the sandbox
orchestrator (``tinycap_sandbox.py``), whose trusted image is stdlib +
pyyaml on purpose and stays that way — so the merge after EvalPlus
conversion runs HERE, as a CPU-only Modal function on this image in the
CLIENT venv (the driver's own environment): ``--merge`` (``--merge-cell-dirs``
narrows it to the converted stores; the orchestrator chains exactly that
command per producing tree). The merge is BOUND to the producing tree:
``--sha`` resolves to the staged tree whose ``TREE_SHA`` names it, and a
store merges only when its ``manifest.producer.tree_sha`` equals that sha
(``partition_by_producer``); a store from another tree is refused when named
explicitly and skipped by the sweep, a legacy store without the field is
refused either way — a store's numbers are never READ through another tree's
``completion.py``. But the producing tree only EMITS (PW10 / E17 A1): its
``completion.complete_task_summaries`` + ``slot_payloads`` write a normalized
payload to a scratch path, and the canonical sourced write is performed by
THIS launcher's own tree (``merge_emitted_payload``) — a tree from before the
source discipline has a writer that overlays payloads and drops the
``sources`` block, and run against today's file it replaced a newer pass's
standing value and erased every source; now no producing tree's writer ever
touches the canonical file (``merge_cell_summaries``).

ISOLATION. Writes ONLY under ``/vol/tinycap/`` (gen, cache, repos,
inspect_evals_cache); ``/vol/objects/scale-12`` (the x1 psr_kl object) and
``/vol/hf`` are read-only shared inputs. At most ``MAX_GPU_CONTAINERS`` (8)
GPU configuration containers without ``--allow-extra`` (the cost
trip-wire). Descriptive container names from the contracts.

Run (from the repo root of a CLEAN, DETACHED checkout at <sha> — ``git
worktree add --detach <dir> <sha>`` — so the launcher process's own mounted
``sisteer`` equals the staged tree, which preflight's
``launcher_modules_match_tree`` refuses otherwise; the tree sha is a RUN
PARAMETER, and every launch prints the exact argv it runs under):
  modal run scripts/modal/tinycap_served.py --sha <sha> --upload-tree --stage --bfcl
  modal run scripts/modal/tinycap_served.py --sha <sha> --pf
  modal run scripts/modal/tinycap_served.py --sha <sha> --smoke          # fitted x off, --limit 5,
                                                          # under <out_dir>/smoke/; --controls gsm8k narrows it
  modal run scripts/modal/tinycap_served.py --sha <sha> --pass1          # the four configurations at
                                                          # their default controls; --cells/--modes/--controls override
  modal run scripts/modal/tinycap_sandbox.py --merge-sha <sha>           # EvalPlus execution, conversion, then
                                                          # the merge below for the converted stores
  modal run scripts/modal/tinycap_served.py --sha <sha> --merge [--merge-cell-dirs a,b]
  python scripts/modal/tinycap_served.py --sha <sha> --pass1 --dry-run    # CPU: print the plan
"""
